WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.123
After the trial Tom was a hero again.

2
00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:07.285
There was a story about him in the town newspaper.

3
00:00:07.286 --> 00:00:11.206
Old people loved him, and young people wanted to be like him.

4
00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:15.788
But Tom didn't feel like a hero because every night he was afraid to go to bed.

5
00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:20.316
In Tom's mind a hero wasn't afraid of the dark.

6
00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:25.953
The fear wasn't so bad during the day when Tom could act like a normal boy.

7
00:00:25.954 --> 00:00:28.188
But his nights were horrible.

8
00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:32.461
Every night he had the same dream: Injun Joe was chasing him.

9
00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:35.385
In the dream Tom ran, and then he fell.

10
00:00:35.386 --> 00:00:39.987
Every night he woke up screaming just as Injun Joe caught him.

11
00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:42.270
Huck was also afraid.

12
00:00:42.271 --> 00:00:47.545
Although Tom hadn't told anyone that Huck saw the murder, Huck was sure it would leak out.

13
00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:51.938
Every day Huck and Tom asked the sheriff if Injun Joe had been caught.

14
00:00:51.939 --> 00:00:55.849
And every day the sheriff said, "No, not yet."

15
00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.515
Huck and Tom were convinced that Injun Joe was waiting to get them.

16
00:01:01.516 --> 00:01:06.550
As the summer drifted along, the boys began to lose some of their fear.

17
00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:12.443
One day, feeling more confident, Tom went looking for someone to help him search for buried treasure.

18
00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:14.881
The only person he found was Huck.

19
00:01:14.882 --> 00:01:19.863
"Hey, Huck," said Tom. "Let's find some buried treasure."

20
00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:23.404
"Sure," said Huck. "Where will we dig?"

21
00:01:23.405 --> 00:01:29.457
"You know, under the roots of old trees, on islands, and of course in haunted houses.

22
00:01:29.458 --> 00:01:37.531
We've already searched one island, so maybe we should look under some dead trees or in the haunted house," answered Tom.

23
00:01:37.532 --> 00:01:40.372
"Who hides treasure?" asked Huck.

24
00:01:40.373 --> 00:01:43.795
"Robbers mostly," answered Tom.

25
00:01:43.796 --> 00:01:47.713
"If I were a robber, I wouldn't hide my treasure," said Huck.

26
00:01:47.714 --> 00:01:50.491
"I'd spend it right away and have a good time."

27
00:01:50.492 --> 00:01:52.876
"Me too," agreed Tom.

28
00:01:52.877 --> 00:01:58.930
"But if robbers weren't stupid, there wouldn't be any treasure for us to find!"

29
00:01:58.931 --> 00:02:05.042
The boys found an old pick and a rusty shovel, and they dug under and around lots of dead trees.

30
00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:07.400
But they didn't have any luck.

31
00:02:07.401 --> 00:02:10.793
"Maybe there are no robbers around here," said Huck.

32
00:02:10.794 --> 00:02:13.047
"That's why we're not finding any treasure."

33
00:02:13.048 --> 00:02:18.553
"No, that's not it. We must be doing something wrong."

34
00:02:18.554 --> 00:02:23.005
Tom thought for a while and then he said, "I know what's wrong!

35
00:02:23.006 --> 00:02:25.730
We need to dig at night."

36
00:02:25.731 --> 00:02:28.416
"We need to dig at night?" asked Huck.

37
00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:39.510
"Yes, treasure maps always say, 'When the moon is high in the sky, walk forty paces and dig under the shadow of the biggest branch,'" answered Tom.

38
00:02:39.511 --> 00:02:44.233
"We need to dig again tonight."

39
00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:49.671
Huck and Tom continued their search for buried treasure that night, but they still had no luck.

40
00:02:49.672 --> 00:02:52.394
"I don't understand," said Huck.

41
00:02:52.395 --> 00:02:57.962
"We marked the shadows of the trees' biggest branches, and we still haven't found any treasure."

42
00:02:57.963 --> 00:03:03.127
"We didn't spot the shadows right at midnight," Tom pointed out.

43
00:03:03.128 --> 00:03:06.501
"We've got to give this up, Tom," said Huck.

44
00:03:06.502 --> 00:03:10.405
But Tom wasn't quite ready to abandon the idea of finding treasure.

45
00:03:10.406 --> 00:03:13.640
"There's still one place we can look, Huck."

46
00:03:13.641 --> 00:03:18.030
"No, Tom, I don't like haunted houses," said Huck.

47
00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:21.220
"We won't look tonight," said Tom.

48
00:03:21.221 --> 00:03:24.505
"Everyone knows that ghosts are dangerous at night.

49
00:03:24.506 --> 00:03:27.619
We can look in the haunted house tomorrow."

50
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.330
"Well, okay," answered Huck.

51
00:03:30.331 --> 00:03:34.331
"As long as you're sure that we won't see a ghost."

52
00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:39.313
"Have you ever heard of someone seeing a ghost during the day?" asked Tom.

53
00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:46.600
"Well, no." Huck seemed satisfied, so he agreed to meet Tom by the haunted house the next afternoon.

54
00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:50.596
As the boys walked back to town, they passed the haunted house.

55
00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:59.407
It stood alone in the middle of a moonlit valley, completely dark and evil-looking.

56
00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:03.817
The next day around noon, the two boys met at the haunted house.

57
00:04:03.818 --> 00:04:09.001
The house was still dark and dreary, but it no longer seemed as evil.

58
00:04:09.002 --> 00:04:14.842
Tom and Huck were about to enter the house when Huck suddenly asked, "What day is it today?"

59
00:04:14.843 --> 00:04:18.431
"It's Friday," answered Tom.

60
00:04:18.432 --> 00:04:22.057
"Did you say Friday?" asked Huck.

61
00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:25.054
"I don't think we should go to the haunted house today."

62
00:04:25.055 --> 00:04:31.123
"Friday's an unlucky day to start a new enterprise," Tom agreed.

63
00:04:31.124 --> 00:04:34.146
He suggested that they play Robin Hood instead.

64
00:04:34.147 --> 00:04:38.438
Huck didn't know who Robin Hood was, so Tom explained it to him.

65
00:04:38.439 --> 00:04:46.730
While the boys played, two pairs of sinister eyes watched them closely from the haunted house.

